Time Complexityenqueue(x): O(1) - Just a single s.push(x).dequeue(): O(n) - In the worst case, it pops all n elements recursively until it reaches the bottom, then pushes them back while unwinding recursion.front(): O(n) - Similar to dequeue(), it traverses all elements recursively to reach the bottom and then restores them.size(): O(1) - Direct call to s.size().Auxiliary Space: O(n) due to the recursion call stack holding up to n elements temporarily.
